  "question": {
    "text": "Which one of the following species is stable in aqueous solution?"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><msubsup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo></mrow></msubsup></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><msubsup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>-</mo></mrow></msubsup></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">u</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>In <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><msubsup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo></mrow></msubsup></math>, manganese is in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn></math> oxidation state, which is having the highest stability.<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msubsup><mtext>MnO</mtext><mn>4</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>&#8658;&#8203;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Cu</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></math>&nbsp; It will disproportionate&nbsp;in aqueous solution.<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Cr</mi><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></math>&nbsp;It will also disproportionate&nbsp;in aqueous solution.<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msubsup><mi>MnO</mi><mn>4</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></math>&nbsp;Mn is not stable in +5 oxidation state.<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></math><br />Higher the oxidation state, more is the stability of the species.</p></blockquote>"
  }
